# Nothing a sample PRODUCES belongs in this repository. A render of a stems export is hundreds of
# megabytes and an extraction cache is more, and both are reproducible from the download they came
# from. The samples themselves refuse an output folder inside the repository; this is the second
# line of defence, for the times somebody points one here by hand anyway.

renders/
render/
output/
out/
cache/
stems-cache/
sample-proof/
tmp/

# Audio and MIDI, wherever under samples/ they land. A sample's source is code and text; anything
# that sounds came from somewhere else and is not ours to carry.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
*.ogg
*.opus
*.mid
*.midi
*.sf2
*.sfz
*.dspreset
*.dslibrary
*.dsbundle
